    "body": "It’s that time of year again, where thousands of soldiers, industry figures, foreign officials and general tank- and helicopter-lovers flood to the Walter E. Washington Convention Center in Washington, DC, for the annual AUSA conference. Land Warfare Reporter Carley Welch and Editor-in-Chief Aaron Mehta run down some of the biggest stories from the day, including what Acting Army Secretary Adam Telle said in his largest address to soldiers and industry since taking on the role.\nThen the two discuss a swarm of balloons sent by the Army to the Middle East. Plus, they make their predictions for what’s still to come at the show.\nBe sure to check back each day for more wrap-up videos from the show. And you can find the rest of our coverage here .",
